{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/354907-when-do-you-spend-experience-points","id":354907,"title":"When do YOU spend Experience Points?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-30T11:14:00-08:00","id":354907,"title":"When do YOU spend Experience Points?","content":"This is an odd question coming from a guy who's been playing cWoD since 1996, but after some thought I decided to throw it out there.<br /> I've always let players spend XP at the end of each story, because somewhere at the back of my mind that was how I first read it back in Vampire: The Masquerade 2nd Edition.<br /> Now all these years later I happened to glance over Experience Point expenditure in a few core books and, lo and behold it doesn't really give a &quot;when&quot; anywhere.<br /> When do you Storytellers allow experience to be spent?<br /> End of each story?<br /> End of each chapter?<br /> Whenever the player wants?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T11:54:03-08:00","id":354931,"title":"","content":"I usually play games of only a few sessions, where advancement isn't generally a factor. When I do play chronicle-style games, I allow players to spend exp in pretty much any period of downtime -whenever they're in a safe and peaceful environment for a day or longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T12:00:04-08:00","id":354936,"title":"","content":"Whenever it makes sense, though rarely in the middle of a scene. Mostly because that would involve a break in the flow of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T12:15:55-08:00","id":354996,"title":"","content":"I usually let my players spend their XP in between stories. I also gauge the downtime on what they choose to spend it on. That is when they get to bluebook. Usually, they will bluebook what they spend the XP on (I spend a few weeks on the gun range to explain why I am giving myself a dot in Firearms).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T12:55:48-08:00","id":355038,"title":"","content":"Echoing sentiments above, generally between stories. Though sometimes, if it makes sense during a session they might be able to spend XP. For example, if we have some time pass in game over the course of a session. Things like Willpower or Rage can sometimes be rationalized in response to an event or trauma the character went through during session.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, I was in a couple of long running Vampire games a few years back where the ST allowed us to spend XP to spontaneously raise in-clan disciplines. Or to instantly spend XP if someone committed diablerie to gain abilities or disciplines the victim had (this was rare, but it happened). But those tend to be exceptions rather than the rule. In those games some of the players (1 was particularly bad about it) horded XP so it allowed for a reason to spend large amounts at once that we couldn\u2019t normally rationalize the time to have spent. The 1 player in question for a long while (6 months of weekly games) didn't spend any I don\u2019t think, and had around 80 XP set aside. I remember him dumping most of it to get out of a deadly situation (during the first Anarch Revolt) by developing 2 level 6 Vicissitude powers. It might\u2019ve been overkill, but that\u2019s besides the point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T15:21:25-08:00","id":355175,"title":"","content":"When I have enough to buy whatever it is I want. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Basically the idea is that a lot of the study is happening both on and off camera. I tend to ask my players to designate the things they are wanting to increase, and then help to toy around with it in game. So, essentially, any time they are awarded XP is also a suitable time for them to spend that XP. I don't give XP in the middle of a combat or half way through a party, so no worries that they suddenly have new Disciplines or extra dice springing up out of nowhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T00:23:43-08:00","id":355518,"title":"","content":"I, and other St's around these parts that I know of, allow XP expenditure between games sessions either at the end of the evenings session or at the beginning of the next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T05:30:06-08:00","id":360156,"title":"","content":"Cool.<br /> Thanks guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T05:45:05-08:00","id":360159,"title":"","content":"Usually at the end of each chapter I make use of some &quot;downtime&quot; when the characters somewhat live they normal lives (or unlives, or undeath or whatever) and can then study, approach normal human (thus making Contact, Followers, Allies and what else) better themselves and learn supernatural tricks. It's in the downtime that they get wild, spen exp and acquire all the trait that make me insane when projecting a story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode